      "role": "user",
      "content": "hey, quick question. i'm a freelancer and i just bought a really expensive ergonomic office chair for my home studio. do i count that as a business expense or is that more like a personal draw? i'm trying to get my quickbooks sorted for the year.",
      "source": "evaluator"
    },
    {
      "role": "assistant",
      "content": "For a freelancer, the ergonomic chair is generally considered a business expense, provided you use it primarily for your work. You can usually deduct the cost as office equipment or furniture. It's a good idea to keep all your receipts, just in case the tax authorities ask for proof of your business use. Remember, if you use it for both work and personal lounging, you might need to prorate the deduction, but for a dedicated home studio setup, it should be straightforward.",
