      "role": "user",
      "content": "makes sense. it's just a bit stressful trying to track everything. i've also noticed that some of my smaller software subscriptions and random supplies seem to just... vanish from my mental checklist or get lost in the shuffle of my bank statements. it feels like money is just leaking out of my accounts and i can't find where it went. is there a good way to keep a tighter grip on those small, irregular costs so they don't disappear on me?",
      "source": "evaluator"
    },
    {
      "role": "assistant",
      "content": "The \"leaking money\" feeling is very common, especially with those tiny, recurring subscriptions! To keep a tighter grip on those small, irregular costs, you need a system that is as organized as a well-managed bank account, which is where the proper use of QuickBooks comes in.\n\nFirst, categorize everything immediately as it comes in, even if it's just a $5 subscription for a niche font or a pack of sticky notes. Use specific tags or categories in QuickBooks for these \"miscellaneous\" items. Secondly, set up automated rules or bank feeds to pull transactions directly into your accounting software, which helps prevent them from getting lost in the raw bank statement noise. This proactive tracking is key to stopping those little expenses from sneaking up on you.",
